s","options":["thrust","roll","pitch","yaw"],"answer":"C","why":"Rotation about the lateral axis."},{"step":"eng-aeronautic","topic":"Aeronautical Engineering","prompt":"A turbofan engine produces most of its thrust from","options":["rockets","the exhaust of the core alone","a propeller","the bypass air moved by the large fan"],"answer":"D","why":"High-bypass engines are efficient at subsonic speeds."},{"step":"eng-aeronautic","topic":"Aeronautical Engineering","prompt":"Composite materials such as carbon-fibre reinforced polymer are used in aircraft because of their","options":["ease of recycling","high strength-to-weight ratio","high density","low cost"],"answer":"B","why":"They save weight and resist fatigue and corrosion."},{"step":"eng-aeronautic","topic":"Aeronautical Engineering","prompt":"Aluminium alloys used in aircraft such as 2024 are strengthened by","options":["precipitation (age) hardening","quenching to form martensite","adding more carbon","cold working only"],"answer":"A","why":"Fine precipitates block dislocation movement."},{"step":"eng-aeronautic","topic":"Aeronautical Engineering","prompt":"Fatigue cracking in aircraft is often found","options":["around rivet holes and other stress concentrations","in parts that carry no load","only in the tyres","only in composite parts"],"answer":"A","why":"Holes concentrate stress."},{"step":"eng-aeronautic","topic":"Aeronautical Engineering","prompt":"Flaps are extended during take-off and landing to","options":["increase speed","control yaw","reduce lift","increase lift at low speed"],"answer":"D","why":"They increase camber and wing area."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Optical fibres carry signals using","options":["sound waves","radio waves","total internal reflection of light","electrical current in copper"],"answer":"C","why":"Light stays in the core because the cladding has a lower refractive index."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"For total internal reflection the light must travel","options":["at exactly 90°","from a higher to a lower refractive index at more than the critical angle","from a lower to a higher refractive index","through air"],"answer":"B","why":"This keeps light inside the core."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Amplitude modulation (AM) varies the","options":["speed of the wave","frequency of the carrier wave","amplitude of the carrier wave","phase only"],"answer":"C","why":"FM varies the frequency."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"An advantage of FM over AM is","options":["longer range over the horizon","uses lower frequencies","simpler circuitry","less affected by electrical noise"],"answer":"D","why":"Noise mainly changes amplitude, which FM ignores."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Geostationary satellites orbit at about","options":["2000 km","36 000 km above the equator","384 000 km","400 km"],"answer":"B","why":"Their period matches Earth's rotation."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Analogue-to-digital conversion involves","options":["modulating a carrier","filtering only","sampling and quantising a signal","amplifying a signal"],"answer":"C","why":"The signal is measured at intervals and given binary values."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Copper is used in telecommunications cable because it has","options":["magnetic properties","very low cost compared with steel","high resistance","high electrical conductivity and ductility"],"answer":"D","why":"It is easily drawn into wire."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Which travels fastest down an optical fibre with lowest loss?","options":["Visible light in multimode fibre over long distances","Radio waves in copper","Infrared light in single-mode fibre","Sound in glass"],"answer":"C","why":"Single-mode fibre avoids modal dispersion."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Mobile phone networks are divided into cells so that","options":["frequencies can be reused in non-adjacent cells","each phone has its own frequency forever","signals travel further","satellites are not needed"],"answer":"A","why":"Frequency reuse increases capacity."},{"step":"eng-telecommun","topic":"Telecommunications Engineering","prompt":"Polyethylene is used to insulate telecommunications cables because it is","options":["a good conductor","brittle","magnetic","a good electrical insulator and water resistant"],"answer":"D","why":"It also flexes without cracking."},{"step":"eng-engineerin","topic":"Engineering Fundamentals","prompt":"Which is a ferrous metal?","options":["Brass","Cast iron","Copper","Aluminium"],"answer":"B","why":"Ferrous metals contain iron."},{"step":"eng-engineerin","topic":"Engineering Fundamentals","prompt":"Ductility is the ability of a material to","options":["conduct heat","be drawn into wire without breaking","break without bending","resist scratching"],"answer":"B","why":"Copper and gold are very ductile."},{"step":"eng-engineerin","topic":"Engineering Fundamentals","prompt":"A third-angle orthogonal drawing places the top view","options":["behind the front view","to the left of the front view","below the front view","above the front view"],"answer":"D","why":"Australian Standard AS 1100 uses third-angle projection."},{"step":"eng-engineerin","topic":"Engineering Fundamentals","prompt":"Hardness is a material's resistance to","options":["indentation and scratching","stretching","bending","impact"],"answer":"A","why":"Measured with Brinell, Vickers or Rockwell tests."},{"step":"eng-engineered","topic":"Engineered Products","prompt":"Injection moulding is best suited to","options":["mass production of identical polymer parts","one-off metal parts","large steel beams","hand-made timber furniture"],"answer":"A","why":"High tooling cost, low cost per part."},{"step":"eng-engineered","topic":"Engineered Products","prompt":"Galvanising protects steel by","options":["coating it with zinc","adding carbon","heating it","painting it red"],"answer":"A","why":"Zinc corrodes in preference to steel."},{"step":"eng-brakingsys","topic":"Braking Systems","prompt":"Disc brakes are better than drum brakes at","options":["dissipating heat","self-energising","working without friction","being cheap"],"answer":"A","why":"The exposed disc cools quickly, reducing brake fade."},{"step":"eng-brakingsys","topic":"Braking Systems","prompt":"Hydraulic brakes rely on","options":["compressed air","magnetism only","pressure transmitted through an incompressible fluid","electrical current"],"answer":"C","why":"Pascal's principle."},{"step":"eng-brakingsys","topic":"Braking Systems","prompt":"Brake fade is caused by","options":["overheating of the brakes","too little friction material","low tyre pressure","cold weather"],"answer":"A","why":"Friction falls as temperature rises."},{"step":"eng-biomedical","topic":"Biomedical Engineering","prompt":"Titanium alloys are used for hip replacements because they are","options":["cheap and magnetic","soft and flexible","transparent","strong, light and biocompatible"],"answer":"D","why":"They also resist corrosion in the body."},{"step":"eng-biomedical","topic":"Biomedical Engineering","prompt":"UHMWPE is used in artificial joints as","options":["a low-friction bearing surface","a structural bone replacement","an electrical conductor","a coating to stop healing"],"answer":"A","why":"It wears slowly against metal or ceramic."}]